1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,253
In the first years

2
00:00:01,253 --> 00:00:02,506
of a thirty-year mortgage,

3
00:00:02,506 --> 00:00:03,759
most of your payment

4
00:00:03,759 --> 00:00:05,012
isn't paying down the

5
00:00:05,012 --> 00:00:05,952
loan at all.

6
00:00:05,952 --> 00:00:07,339
It's mostly going toward

7
00:00:07,339 --> 00:00:08,725
interest, on the full

8
00:00:08,725 --> 00:00:10,112
amount you still owe.

9
00:00:10,112 --> 00:00:11,405
That's how amortization

10
00:00:11,405 --> 00:00:11,836
works.

11
00:00:11,836 --> 00:00:13,560
Every fixed payment is

12
00:00:13,560 --> 00:00:15,283
split between interest and

13
00:00:15,283 --> 00:00:17,007
principal, and early on,

14
00:00:17,007 --> 00:00:18,731
interest wins that split.

15
00:00:18,731 --> 00:00:20,145
As the balance shrinks,

16
00:00:20,145 --> 00:00:21,559
less interest is owed

17
00:00:21,559 --> 00:00:22,973
each month, so more

18
00:00:22,973 --> 00:00:24,387
of the same payment

19
00:00:24,387 --> 00:00:25,801
starts chipping away at

20
00:00:25,801 --> 00:00:26,155
principal.

21
00:00:26,155 --> 00:00:27,516
By the back half

22
00:00:27,516 --> 00:00:28,877
of the loan, the

23
00:00:28,877 --> 00:00:29,898
split flips almost

24
00:00:29,898 --> 00:00:30,238
completely,

25
00:00:30,238 --> 00:00:31,599
and most of the

26
00:00:31,599 --> 00:00:32,620
payment finally builds

27
00:00:32,620 --> 00:00:32,960
equity.

28
00:00:32,960 --> 00:00:34,372
It's not a hidden

29
00:00:34,372 --> 00:00:35,784
fee. It's just how

30
00:00:35,784 --> 00:00:37,197
a fixed loan payment

31
00:00:37,197 --> 00:00:38,609
gets divided over thirty

32
00:00:38,609 --> 00:00:40,021
years. Follow for more.
